From e298fb620b4ffc5e7e90d2f6200e9a25dcde5223 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Kuegel <akuegel@google.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:28:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA] Fix runtime variable ordering when composing indexing
 maps

ComposeIndexingMaps(first, second) orders symbols in the composed IndexingMap
as [range_vars(second), range_vars(first), rt_vars(second), rt_vars(first)].
However, both ComposeOperandIndexing and ComposeInstructionIndexing appended
first's runtime variables before second's runtime variables, causing the
runtime variable bindings to be rotated relative to the composed map's RTVar
domains and affine expressions.

Reorder the runtime variable lists in ComposeOperandIndexing and
ComposeInstructionIndexing to place second's runtime variables before first's.

PiperOrigin-RevId: 985904188
